      "modify_to": "Estimate world positions using calibrated camera rays. Intersect ring-center rays with the tabletop plane z=0. Locate the center of the cube's top face, preferably in the calibrated current wrist image, and intersect its ray with the approximately z=0.04 top-face plane. Do not use the cube's silhouette center or project its image center onto the table. Use the resulting horizontal center for both the z=0.15 pickup approach and the z=0.02 grasp, allowing the stated approach endpoint tolerance. Transform two points along a top-face edge into world coordinates on that plane before deriving grasp yaw; an image-plane edge angle is not world yaw. Orient the hand straight down, roll approximately pi and pitch zero, with yaw aligned to the resulting world horizontal edge direction; maintain that orientation while carrying and releasing it."
    }
  ],
  "refused": "Do not substitute transport, placement contact, or regrasp frames for release-and-separation evidence, or retain the old episode-order label assignments. Do not infer the demonstrated release location from the execution destination: preserve the selected ring's identity through any subsequent shuffle. No execution-history field or episode-specific destination coordinates are added; the existing observable-state motion rules apply to the corrected destination."
}
